body: "The `release` job of the Daily Release workflow failed.\n\n- Failing job: `release`\n- Run URL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/39395169163\n- Commit: fda9c1fbf5420230cfc7ec6b7dae0796262313f2\n- Date (UTC): 2026-10-20T09:06:24Z\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@github-actions[bot]** (2026-10-21T09:00:53Z)\n>\n> The `release` job of the Daily Release workflow failed.\n> \n> - Failing job: `release`\n> - Run URL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/39571254862\n> - Commit: 188a3c62f7390a92b00a590205a86266ca09404d\n> - Date (UTC): 2026-10-21T09:00:51Z\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-21T09:26:08Z)\n>\n> Hosted evidence for today's failure, distinct from release-heading failures:\n> \n> Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/39571254862 (job https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/39571254862/job/119125710807, source 188a3c62f7390a92b00a590205a86266ca09404d) first passed 287/287 coverage tests, then the later release-check invocation failed 1/287 at test/atomic.test.ts:1203: F2 create-overrun recovery. Expected /still open/i, actual diagnostic said the identified orphan was closed. This occurred with exact development CLI2026.10.15, pm-changelog2026.10.16, pm-ops2026.10.16; it is not evidence against latest CLI2026.10.21 or npm publication.\n> \n> Static distinction: the test asserts that a 16-byte buffer always forces recovery-close status=null. The implementation only emits was closed when rc.status===0, so this hosted assertion alone does NOT reproduce a false runtime receipt or prove an orphan was left open. The same test passed in one invocation and failed in another. Fixture nondeterminism is a supported inference from those hosted results and the buffer-cap assumption, not an independently reproduced root cause. Preserve the runtime outcome check; stabilize the test by deterministically inducing and observing the close failure separately from successful recovery.\n> \n> Existing canonical context: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/blob/188a3c62f7390a92b00a590205a86266ca09404d/.agents/pm/issues/pm-csv-158c.toon and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/blob/188a3c62f7390a92b00a590205a86266ca09404d/.agents/pm/issues/pm-csv-yriu.toon require truthful recovery outcomes and deterministic/reaped test writers. Existing issue173 is the release-blocker owner, not a new duplicate issue.\n> \n> Acceptance: force successful and null/nonzero recovery-close outcomes independently; verify exact receipt and item identity for each, reap delegated writers before cleanup; repeat the exact release gate under the pinned toolchain without weakening assertions. No local reproduction or deployed/runtime impact claimed here.\n>"
